Add following line to ~/.bashrc
source ~/dev-shortcuts/bash/extensions.sh

NOTE: change the path of dev-shortcuts to your local path


Recommendations:
- Store kubeconfig for production in a separate file
- Use the default kubeconfig file for local development
- Please refer to bash/dev-config/readme for details.

Prod Commands:
kprod <ns> <verb> [resource] [options]
kprod <ns> <verb> [*<resource>] [options] # *<resource> applies grep on the returned resoruces to filter them out.

if <ns> is not applicable:
Pass on - for <ns>, it will pull the cluster resources

if you want to run raw command:
kprod -- [-n <ns>] <verb> [resource] [options]

Local environment:
- Replace kprod with klocal to use default kubeconfig.
- klocal uses default kubeconfig
- example: klocal <ns> <verb> [resource] [options]
- klocal appropriately switches to use the default kubeconfig

Options:
| -------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Option   | Long Option        | Description                                                                                                                                   |
| -------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `-A`     | `--all-namespaces` | Search across all namespaces.                                                                                                                 |
| -------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `-s`     | `--sort-by`        | Sort resources. <br>Accepts: `a`, `ts`, or `age` (sort by creationTimestamp), `-` (no sort), or any `.field.path`. Default: `.metadata.name`. |
| -------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `-nn`    | `--node-name`      | Filter by node name. Uses Kubernetes field selector `spec.nodeName=<value>`.                                                                  |
| -------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| -p|-g|-r | `--search-pattern` | Pattern to search in logs.                                                                                                                    |
| -------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `-oless` | `-less`            | Show output in `less` with `-oyaml` format.                                                                                                   |
| -------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `-ocode` | `-code`            | Open output in VS Code (`code`) with `-oyaml` format.                                                                                         |
| -------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `-oyaml` |                    | Output format in YAML.                                                                                                                        |
| -------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `-ojson` |                    | Output format in JSON.                                                                                                                        |
| -------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `-l`     |                    | Label selector. Must be in format: `-l key=value`. Cannot be used with resource name.                                                         |
| -------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `-go`    |                    | Language runtime set to `go`. Used to format logs.                                                                                            |
| -------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `-net`   |                    | Language runtime set to `.NET`. Used to format logs.                                                                                          |
| -------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `-w`     | `--watch`          | Enable Kubernetes watch mode.                                                                                                                 |
| -------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `--`     |                    | Signals that the following arguments are direct commands.                                                                                     |
| -------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
|*<pattern>|                    | Wildcard for resource name pattern (e.g., `nginx-*`).                                                                                         |
| -------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |

Demo app proxy retry testing:
- Leader election and non-leader fault injection are disabled by default.
- For fault injection, enable --leader-election --non-leader-action=close/503.
  All pods keep their HTTP/HTTPS ports bound, except in skip-port-binding mode.
- --leader-election-lease-name defaults to demo-app-leader. Use the same lease
  name for participating replicas and a different name for unrelated apps.
- --leader-election-namespace defaults to POD_NAMESPACE or the mounted service
  account namespace. Election uses in-cluster credentials and requires permission
  to create leases and get/update the named lease in coordination.k8s.io.
- GET /keepalive returns HTTP 200 with body "ok" on the leader.
  The action is selected once per request, before reading its body. A close
  action closes the connection immediately without draining the body. Other
  responses drain, discard and close any body first. Body read/close errors
  return HTTP 400; canceled requests stop handling without a response.
  Non-leader behavior is selected by --non-leader-action:
  - none (default): return HTTP 200 with body "ok" without injecting faults.
  - close: close the underlying connection before sending any response.
  - 503: return HTTP 503 with pod identity and leadership state.
  - close/503: independently choose close or HTTP 503 with 50% probability each
    on every request. Non-leaders never return 200 in this mode. Small samples
    are not guaranteed to contain equal numbers of each failure.
  - skip-port-binding: an exclusive alternative to the request-level actions.
    Only the leader binds HTTP/HTTPS ports, including gRPC. Non-leaders leave
    all server ports unbound; leadership loss closes listeners and all existing
    connections, including H2C and WebSockets. Regaining leadership rebinds them.
    Before the first election, no replica binds its server ports.
  Fault injection requires --leader-election. Request-level actions only affect
  /keepalive; other endpoints, including /liveness, /ready, gRPC and WebSockets,
  remain independent of leadership. Closing an HTTP/2 connection also interrupts
  other streams on that connection. Skip-port-binding affects all endpoints and
  cannot be mixed with close/503 or --close-connection-from-non-leader.
- GET /liveness is the separate liveness endpoint and normally returns HTTP 200
  with body "ok". It retains the explicit --fail-liveness-probe and
  --fail-probes-after-seconds options, which do not affect /keepalive.
  Demo app liveness probes use /liveness, not the fault-injection endpoint.
  In skip-port-binding mode, omit HTTP probes on non-leaders because no server
  ports are bound.
- --close-connection-from-non-leader remains a legacy alias for
  --non-leader-action=close; it cannot be combined with a different fault action.
- Before a leader is elected, all replicas are non-leaders and apply the chosen
  fault action. Only skip-port-binding closes/rebinds listeners on role changes.
- Election is per namespace/cluster, not across clusters. Lease duration is 15s,
  renewal deadline 10s, and retry period 2s. Shutdown releases the lease.
- demo-apps/yaml/demo-app-rwpr-fault.yaml enables leader election and the
  skip-port-binding action for two replicas, includes the service account and RBAC, and
  omits readiness/liveness probes. Its proxy retry policy remains disabled;
  configure retries on the proxy separately to test recovery.
- Example: curl -v http://<pod-ip>:12012/keepalive
  A leader responds with 200; a non-leader leaves its ports unbound in
  skip-port-binding mode. In close/503 mode, a non-leader either closes the
  connection without a response or returns 503. A retrying proxy can retry
  another backend, but success depends on its retry policy and backend selection.
